====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cause]] to [[float]] with the tide; to [[drive]] or [[carry]] with the tide or stream.
#* {{RQ:Feltham Resolves|passage=They are '''tided''' down the stream.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[pour]] a tide or flood.
#: ''The ocean '''tided''' most impressively.''
# {{lb|en|intransitive|nautical}} To work into or out of a river or harbor by drifting with the tide and anchoring when it becomes adverse.

